  routed via edge: yes

  No /etc/hosts needed for curl — send the Host header, over HTTPS (the edge
  serves TLS on this port under --public-ingress; -k because it is self-signed).
  Every one of these was documented as http:// and returned nothing at all:

    curl -k -H 'Host: app.forge.run'   https://127.0.0.1:8081/
    curl -k -H 'Host: forge.run'       https://127.0.0.1:8081/
    curl -k -H 'Host: ws-30bb36de.forge.run' https://127.0.0.1:8081/platform/metrics

  /platform/metrics is also served, in plain HTTP, on the workspace runtime's
  own port — the address to reach for when the edge is not what you are
  testing. It is in dev/run/state/ports.json:

    curl http://127.0.0.1:40000/platform/metrics

  For a browser, add to /etc/hosts (needs sudo):

    127.0.0.1  forge.run app.forge.run auth.forge.run code.forge.run status.forge.run

  ...then browse to http://forge.run:8081/

  The workspace is EMPTY until you deploy — until then every declarative route
  404s from the runtime ("no route for GET /"). Routing being correct and the
  portal rendering are separate problems. To deploy the portal:

    cd /Users/rory/Documents/forge-run/forge-portal-web
    forge build                                    # wasm + forge.lock
    git remote add forge-local \
      http://127.0.0.1:8010/ws-30bb36de/forge-portal-web
    git push forge-local <branch>:main             # → derive → converge

  A push needs a workspace admin bearer. Bootstrap one once (loopback only):

    curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:40000/api/v1/manage/users/bootstrap \
      -H 'content-type: application/json' \
      -d '{"email":"dev@forge.run","password":"…","role":"admin"}'

